{ Tests for PascalCommon.Cache: the memory store (expiry on a manual ticker,
  eviction of the expired then the oldest, Delete, a TTL of 0, capacity 0
  keeping nothing and no tag counters, bounded tag counters that come back
  larger), and TPcCache (the store key's shape and that it is unambiguous,
  invalidation by either tag, the metrics, GetOrLoad's single-flight with
  its loader running once for concurrent misses and its exception reaching
  every thread, and the failure policy: a miss, an ignored Put, OnError, the
  pause and the retry, '' keys, and a store bug that propagates).

  Expiry and the pause run on a manual TTicker; no test sleeps to let time
  pass. The concurrent tests block the loader on an event and release it
  only once every other thread is waiting for it (TPcCache.LoadsWaiting), so
  "the loader ran once" doesn't depend on scheduling; every wait has a
  deadline. Each test uses a cache name of its own, so its metrics start at
  0 in the process-wide PcMetrics.

